00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:03.219
Hey youtubers, it’s Charlie.

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:09.360
Hopefully everyone’s had a chance to see
Episode 9 and process a little.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.839
Because Ra’s Al Ghul is such a big thing
this season I wanted to do a bonus breakdown

00:00:12.839 --> 00:00:17.119
of the most important stories I think you
should read and an explanation of the Lazarus

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:18.320
Pit.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.920
He’s appeared in over 500 Issues, and not
all of them were Batman Titles.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.900
But most of his best stories are Batman stories.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.310
I tried to pick stories I think are really
good and are relevant to what’s happening

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.480
on the show.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.110
So general spoiler warning for Arrow episode
9.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.930
Here we go, Top 5 Ra’s Al Ghul Stories.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.790
Number 5 - Tales Of The Demon Collected Edition

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.780
Number 4 - Death And The Maidens

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.430
Number 3 - Tower Of Babel

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.930
Number 2 - Birth of The Demon Trilogy

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.000
Number 1 - Daughter Of The Demon

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.090
Now just to explain the Lazarus Pit a little
more.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:59.890
Ra’s Al Ghul’s origin story explains that
he found the pits as a young man completely

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.940
by accident while trying to save a prince’s
life.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.350
He was completely healed, but as a side effect,
left completely insane and ended up killing

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.350
Ra’s wife.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:16.620
Ra’s was framed for the murder and given
the death sentence of being forced to wander

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.620
the desert.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.440
He found help and eventually began to use
the Lazarus Pits over and over.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:25.040
There was a pit called the Fountain of Essence
that had different effects.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.900
It healed Ra’s Al Ghul after he’d been
dead for a long time.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.150
He didn’t go insane, but he did come back
in a really old feeble body.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.210
Batman used it when he had minor wounds and
it de-aged him a little.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:45.270
Another character was with them and when he
tried to use the Fountain it killed him.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.730
So not all the pits are the same.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:52.420
But usually when someone refers to the Lazarus
Pit, they’re referring to the traditional

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.420
ones.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.690
And yes, there are many all over the world
in the comics.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:00.580
There was even a period where Batman and Bane
traveled around trying to destroy them all

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:07.260
so Ra’s wouldn’t be able to keep healing
himself.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.829
But as expected there were a bunch of hidden
ones they never found.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:14.110
There have been a ton of characters that have
used a Lazarus Pit including:

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:25.279
Black Canary, she used it to restore her Canary
Cry powers and her ability to bear children.

00:02:25.279 --> 00:04:09.809
Nyssa Al Ghul 
used 

00:04:09.809 --> 00:04:22.750
them 

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.990
to stay young and to warp Talia’s mind.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:30.950
She’d kill her and heal her over and over
to brainwash her.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:36.250
Lady Shiva, Dick Grayson, The Riddler and
Mr Freeze have all taken advantage.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.600
Because Arrow is really conservative with
how they do superpowers, it’s possible we

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.430
could see a twist on the idea of resurrection.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:45.879
Oliver seemed like he should have died when
he tumbled off the cliff.

00:04:45.879 --> 00:04:49.970
But in the promo for episode 10 we see someone
approaching his body.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.130
Clearly he’s going to come back.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.889
So what I think will happen is someone will
just nurse him back to health and use some

00:04:56.889 --> 00:04:58.060
extra powerful techniques.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.919
I don’t think we’ll see the traditional
Lazarus Pit.

00:05:00.919 --> 00:05:08.560
I do think we’ll see some easter eggs, the
show will acknowledge it, but I don’t think

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:14.759
Oliver will be bathing in green fire anytime
soon.

00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:17.759
A lot of people have pointed out Malcolm Merlyn’s
necklace here.

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:21.979
The Green Vial as being a potential easter
egg for the Pit.

00:05:21.979 --> 00:05:26.710
It’s possible he’s the person we see in
the promo and he’ll save Oliver as a way

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:33.229
to repay him for wiping his debt with the
League.

00:05:33.229 --> 00:05:37.860
John Barrowman made some comments about filming
Episode 9 and he said he was in a very cold,

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:38.860
windy place.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.980
Implying that he was filming scenes on that
mountain top set.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.759
Since we didn’t see him there in the episode,
the evidence points to him being the person

00:05:45.759 --> 00:05:46.759
right here.

00:05:46.759 --> 00:06:01.960
Let me know if you agree, do you think Malcolm
Merlyn will 

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:16.669
be the one 

00:06:16.669 --> 00:06:22.949
to save Oliver?

